1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:03,460
Last time, we learnt that a magnet has two poles, where its

2
00:00:03,480 --> 00:00:05,000
pull is strongest.

3
00:00:05,470 --> 00:00:07,350
The top ring floats on a push.

4
00:00:07,800 --> 00:00:09,690
But turn it over, and it pulls!

5
00:00:10,874 --> 00:00:13,384
A little lizard is hiding in this video.

6
00:00:13,634 --> 00:00:14,874
Can you spot it?

7
00:00:14,996 --> 00:00:16,226
Look up high!

8
00:00:16,354 --> 00:00:18,194
Lock in first with your fingers.

9
00:00:18,464 --> 00:00:20,294
One finger for every point.

10
00:00:20,881 --> 00:00:22,211
Today you'll learn:

11
00:00:22,408 --> 00:00:24,108
Unlike and like poles.

12
00:00:24,313 --> 00:00:25,883
Why the ring floats.

13
00:00:26,080 --> 00:00:27,430
Is it a magnet?

14
00:00:29,035 --> 00:00:29,915
Round one.

15
00:00:30,215 --> 00:00:32,185
Two bar magnets push apart.

16
00:00:32,625 --> 00:00:34,395
Basil turns one of them round.

17
00:00:34,685 --> 00:00:35,735
What happens?

18
00:00:36,005 --> 00:00:37,815
One, they still push apart.

19
00:00:38,085 --> 00:00:39,615
Two, they pull together.

20
00:00:39,915 --> 00:00:41,445
Three, nothing happens.

21
00:00:41,715 --> 00:00:43,085
Show me your fingers.

22
00:00:48,554 --> 00:00:49,534
Locked in!

23
00:00:49,662 --> 00:00:50,402
Two!

24
00:00:50,502 --> 00:00:53,662
When Basil turned the ring over, the push became a pull.

25
00:00:53,710 --> 00:00:56,820
One! It is the same magnet, just turned round.

26
00:00:56,990 --> 00:00:58,340
So it still pushes!

27
00:00:58,614 --> 00:01:00,134
Be a toy train carriage!

28
00:01:00,424 --> 00:01:01,404
Shrink down.

29
00:01:01,684 --> 00:01:02,614
Quietly.

30
00:01:04,903 --> 00:01:08,253
You are a toy train carriage, with a small magnet at each

31
00:01:08,273 --> 00:01:08,853
end.

32
00:01:09,643 --> 00:01:11,343
Ahead of you is the engine.

33
00:01:11,860 --> 00:01:13,020
Roll closer.

34
00:01:13,810 --> 00:01:15,730
The engine rolls away from you!

35
00:01:16,500 --> 00:01:17,830
You never touch it.

36
00:01:18,600 --> 00:01:20,430
Something is pushing it away.

37
00:01:20,951 --> 00:01:22,601
Basil turns you round.

38
00:01:23,401 --> 00:01:25,821
Now your other end faces the engine.

39
00:01:26,601 --> 00:01:28,351
Roll closer, and click!

40
00:01:29,141 --> 00:01:30,351
You pull together.

41
00:01:30,857 --> 00:01:32,917
Same carriage, same engine.

42
00:01:33,677 --> 00:01:36,687
Only the end facing the engine has changed.

43
00:01:38,349 --> 00:01:40,699
The answer is two: they pull together!

44
00:01:40,949 --> 00:01:42,529
Did you show two fingers?

45
00:01:42,769 --> 00:01:44,168
Put one finger up!

46
00:01:44,188 --> 00:01:45,038
I know!

47
00:01:45,178 --> 00:01:48,748
When two magnets push apart, they must both be North poles.

48
00:01:48,808 --> 00:01:49,728
Right?

49
00:01:50,380 --> 00:01:51,510
Look closer.

50
00:01:52,100 --> 00:01:55,820
Two bar magnets: North is red, and South is blue.

51
00:01:56,400 --> 00:01:59,314
North pole to South pole: they pull together.

52
00:01:59,334 --> 00:02:02,504
Unlike poles means poles that are not the same, such as a

53
00:02:02,524 --> 00:02:04,344
North pole and a South pole.

54
00:02:04,584 --> 00:02:06,274
Unlike poles attract!

55
00:02:06,852 --> 00:02:09,772
North pole to North pole: they push apart.

56
00:02:10,342 --> 00:02:12,312
And South pole to South pole?

57
00:02:12,902 --> 00:02:14,296
They push apart too!

58
00:02:14,316 --> 00:02:17,496
Like poles means poles that are the same, such as North and

59
00:02:17,516 --> 00:02:19,486
North, or South and South.

60
00:02:19,786 --> 00:02:21,106
Like poles repel!

61
00:02:21,680 --> 00:02:23,290
Now look at Pip's rings.

62
00:02:23,840 --> 00:02:28,090
In our picture, the two faces that meet are both North poles.

63
00:02:28,660 --> 00:02:31,554
Like poles repel, so the top ring floats.

64
00:02:31,574 --> 00:02:34,654
Turn it over, and a South pole meets a North pole.

65
00:02:35,244 --> 00:02:38,044
Unlike poles attract, so it snaps down.

66
00:02:40,755 --> 00:02:42,005
Say it with me!

67
00:02:42,716 --> 00:02:45,596
Unlike poles attract and like poles repel.

68
00:02:48,872 --> 00:02:49,782
Showdown!

69
00:02:50,082 --> 00:02:51,212
Double points.

70
00:02:51,472 --> 00:02:53,392
Pip's homework has one mistake.

71
00:02:53,672 --> 00:02:55,452
Line one, two, or three?

72
00:02:55,742 --> 00:02:57,212
Show me with your fingers.

73
00:02:57,273 --> 00:02:59,843
One: a North pole attracted a South pole.

74
00:03:00,013 --> 00:03:02,453
Two: two South poles pushed apart.

75
00:03:02,653 --> 00:03:05,883
Three: my magnet attracted the iron nail, so the nail is a

76
00:03:05,903 --> 00:03:06,823
magnet.

77
00:03:12,431 --> 00:03:13,411
Locked in!

78
00:03:13,539 --> 00:03:14,289
Three!

79
00:03:14,379 --> 00:03:17,829
My magnet attracts iron nails and steel paper clips, and they are

80
00:03:17,849 --> 00:03:19,069
not magnets.

81
00:03:19,299 --> 00:03:21,249
Being attracted does not prove it!

82
00:03:22,422 --> 00:03:23,512
Three fingers?

83
00:03:23,752 --> 00:03:25,682
Put up two more on your score hand!

84
00:03:25,882 --> 00:03:28,732
Then how can I prove that something is a magnet?

85
00:03:29,382 --> 00:03:30,532
Look closer.

86
00:03:31,112 --> 00:03:34,192
These two grey bars look exactly the same.

87
00:03:34,772 --> 00:03:36,142
One is a magnet.

88
00:03:36,722 --> 00:03:38,996
The other is just a bar of iron.

89
00:03:39,016 --> 00:03:42,386
Basil's magnet pulls both bars, at both ends.

90
00:03:42,956 --> 00:03:46,440
So being pulled does not tell us which one is the magnet.

91
00:03:46,460 --> 00:03:48,630
Now turn Basil's magnet round.

92
00:03:49,220 --> 00:03:51,450
One end of bar B pushes it away!

93
00:03:52,020 --> 00:03:53,515
Bar A never pushes.

94
00:03:53,535 --> 00:03:55,225
Bar B repelled my magnet.

95
00:03:55,265 --> 00:03:56,831
So bar B is the magnet!

96
00:03:56,851 --> 00:03:58,401
That is the repel test!

97
00:03:58,471 --> 00:04:00,911
If it repels a magnet, it is a magnet.

98
00:04:00,961 --> 00:04:02,841
Being pulled is not enough.

99
00:04:06,143 --> 00:04:07,293
Say it with me!

100
00:04:08,007 --> 00:04:10,777
A magnet can attract or repel another magnet.

101
00:04:11,317 --> 00:04:14,547
You can confirm that an object is a magnet if it repels

102
00:04:14,567 --> 00:04:15,817
another magnet.

103
00:04:18,575 --> 00:04:19,680
Say it with us!

104
00:04:20,340 --> 00:04:21,535
Unlike poles?

105
00:04:21,920 --> 00:04:22,847
Attract!

106
00:04:26,740 --> 00:04:27,890
Like poles?

107
00:04:28,320 --> 00:04:29,210
Repel!

108
00:04:33,140 --> 00:04:34,697
Does it repel a magnet?

109
00:04:34,720 --> 00:04:36,207
Then it is a magnet!

110
00:04:40,295 --> 00:04:41,755
Show me your score hand!

111
00:04:42,035 --> 00:04:43,485
Two fingers or more?

112
00:04:43,775 --> 00:04:45,135
You beat the Buddies.

113
00:04:45,425 --> 00:04:46,495
Three fingers?

114
00:04:46,775 --> 00:04:47,775
High five!

115
00:04:47,978 --> 00:04:49,378
Did you spot the lizard?

116
00:04:49,678 --> 00:04:52,668
It was upside down on the ceiling, above the fridge!

117
00:04:52,809 --> 00:04:54,289
Here is a fun fact!

118
00:04:54,389 --> 00:04:58,169
A lizard's toes are covered with tiny hairs, too small to see.

119
00:04:58,219 --> 00:05:01,609
They help it hold on, even upside down on the ceiling, with

120
00:05:01,629 --> 00:05:03,509
no glue and no magnet!

121
00:05:03,632 --> 00:05:04,912
Tell someone at home!

122
00:05:05,951 --> 00:05:09,811
Next time: Basil hangs his bar magnet on a string, so it

123
00:05:09,831 --> 00:05:11,001
can turn freely.

124
00:05:11,271 --> 00:05:13,021
He spins it again and again.

125
00:05:13,301 --> 00:05:14,431
Where does it stop?

126
00:05:14,741 --> 00:05:16,801
One, a different way every time.

127
00:05:17,071 --> 00:05:19,101
Two, the same way every time.

128
00:05:19,381 --> 00:05:20,701
Lock in your answer!

129
00:05:20,975 --> 00:05:23,175
Let's read today's key words together!

130
00:05:23,465 --> 00:05:24,225
Ready?

131
00:05:24,512 --> 00:05:25,712
Unlike poles.

132
00:05:27,352 --> 00:05:28,482
Like poles.

133
00:05:30,044 --> 00:05:31,314
The repel test.

134
00:05:32,964 --> 00:05:33,904
Well done!

135
00:05:34,886 --> 00:05:35,987
Say it with us!

136
00:05:36,787 --> 00:05:37,537
Ready?

137
00:05:37,660 --> 00:05:38,320
One!

138
00:05:38,660 --> 00:05:39,360
two!

139
00:05:39,665 --> 00:05:40,840
Now you know!
